   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "About training",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 3. Training\n\nComfyUI's own **Train LoRA** node on **Krea 2 Raw** (`krea2_raw_fp8_scaled.safetensors`), the undistilled model Krea released to be fine-tuned. The FP8 weights stay frozen; **bypass_mode** attaches the LoRA through hooks, which is what lets a 12.9B model train on one 32-48 GB GPU.\n\nStarting point for a 15-30 image character set: **rank 16, learning rate 0.0001, 1500 steps**, batch 1. More images -> more steps. Out of memory: turn **offloading** on (slower).\n\n**Loss graph**: `output/krea2_lora/loss_graph_*.png`. It should fall and then flatten; a curve that keeps rising means the learning rate is too high.\n\n**Continue a run**: pick the saved LoRA in `existing_lora` and queue again with more steps."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    2640,
    1874
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    420
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 5,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "About the test",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 4. Test on Turbo\n\nThe new LoRA goes straight onto **Krea 2 Turbo** (8 steps, the model the other workflows use) and renders the test prompts in **Test prompts**. Use your trigger word in them.\n\nThe LoRA is saved to `ComfyUI/output/loras/` and shows up in every LoRA loader. In the other workflows, add a **LoraLoaderModelOnly** after *Load Krea 2 Turbo* (or enable the Style LoRA node in the single-image workflow and pick your LoRA). Strength 0.8-1.0."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
